components.reason:
OAW notes cite code, but nothing checks those citations, so drift between a note and current code is left to the agent's judgement. Stdlib re-implementation:
- parse backticked `rel/path.py::Name[::Member]` in docs/raw and docs/knowledge;
- resolve the path with confined_path;
- for .py files, confirm with ast that a def or class of that name exists;
- classify each citation as path-resolved (EXTRACTED) or bare (INFERRED);
- unlike graphify, report ambiguous or unresolved citations as warnings (errors under --strict) rather than dropping them.
It is deterministic, adds no dependency, and its fixture tests are free. This is the wiki duel's Step 0.

components.what:
graphify's hook engineering, good and bad.
Good practice:
- an explicit 10s timeout instead of the host's 600s default;
- hooks that fail open;
- a per-agent nudge budget (session_id plus hashed agent_id; the first nudge always fires; a fresh query stamp silences later ones; cap 5; markers garbage-collected after 24h);
- a strict deny claimed at most once per session with O_EXCL;
- factual rather than imperative wording;
- repository text flattened to one inert line;
- command parsing that understands tokens;
- hook blocks run in a subshell so `exit 0` does not end other tools' hook code;
- skips for linked worktrees and rebases;
- removal of only its own hook entries rather than whole groups.
Anti-patterns:
- breaking away from the parent job object;
- absolute paths in committed config;
- a no-op hook with no timeout.

detect.py silently skips these credential-bearing files:
- .env and .envrc variants;
- *.pem, .key, .p12, .pfx, .crt, .der and .p8;
- id_rsa, id_dsa, id_ecdsa and id_ed25519 (matched with a left boundary);
- secring;
- .netrc, .pgpass, .htpasswd, .npmrc, .pypirc, .git-credentials and .boto.
redact_secrets strips credential-shaped text from labels.

components.reason:
OAW has no structural code map, so this can only ever be a pack. Core is ruled out by the stdlib-only rule, the v2 ban on graph memory and the 24 KB skill gate.
Permitted use until tested:
- a pinned graphifyy installed by the user in its own venv or pipx, at project scope;
- GRAPHIFY_BACKEND=none and GRAPHIFY_NO_AUTO_REFRESH=1;
- no skill, no `claude install`, no `hook install`;
- graphify-out/ gitignored;
- never `export wiki` into docs/.
It complements the LLM wiki (judge) and is not vector retrieval. Its own detector says corpora under 50k words may not need a graph. The upstream benchmarks are not evidence: n=6, the harness is absent, and they describe hybrid and embedding setups this SHA does not ship.
